        "text_Urc8Hy": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>If you want a pet accessory that seamlessly blends play, comfort, and style, a cat cube is your best bet. Over my 10 years working with feline behavior and home pet products, I’ve seen cats instantly gravitate toward cube-shaped hideaways—both for the privacy they offer and the sense of control they create.</p><p>Sexy Liza’s Pop Up Tent Cat Cube from Snarky Pets delivers exactly that. Measuring ~24″ long × 22″ high × 20″ wide, with a generous 14-inch entry hole, a neutral yet elegant design, mesh panels for airflow and visibility, and a lightweight collapsible structure—it’s perfect for cats that love lounging, hiding, or just observing their domain. In this article, I’ll explain why cubical hideouts are one of the best accessories you can get, compare with competitor options, and give you tips to choose, place, and enjoy a cat cube that makes both you and your cat happy. Let’s get started.</p>"
          }
        }
