    "rich_text_xbFPbM": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_ynjcCq": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<strong>Why the Cat Cube Is a Perfect Choice for Indoor Cats</strong>",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_faVBT6": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Cats love enclosed spaces because they feel safe. A cube provides four walls and a roof with an entrance that allows retreat. This satisfies their instinct to hide, rest, and watch without distractions.</p><ul><li><br/><strong>Privacy & Security:</strong> Cats often pick cube hideouts to nap or observe from behind secure walls. It gives shy or anxious cats a place to decompress.<br/></li><li><br/><strong>Ventilation & Visibility:</strong> Good cubes use mesh panels or vents so the cube doesn’t feel stuffy or isolating. Sexy Liza’s cube includes durable mesh windows that let your cat see out and you check in.<br/></li><li><br/><strong>Space Efficiency:</strong> The cube’s dimensions (24×22×20 in) offer plenty of room without being bulky. It fits bedrooms, corners, or near windows.<br/></li><li><br/><strong>Multi-Function Use:</strong> Cubes aren’t just beds; they’re observation posts, hiding spots, and play zones.</li></ul>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_ynjcCq",
        "text_faVBT6"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.rich-text.presets.name",
      "settings": {
        "desktop_content_position": "center",
        "content_alignment": "center",
        "color_scheme": "",
        "full_width": true,
