    "rich_text_8atpqp": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_7jTBtL": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<strong>How to Choose the Right Cat Cube for You & Your Cat</strong>",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_cE7LyU": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>From my experience, these features are the ones you should prioritize:</p><ul><li><br/><strong>Entry size</strong>: For larger cats, ensure the hole is at least ~14 in diameter.<br/></li><li><br/><strong>Interior room</strong>: Enough space to stretch, rest, or stand under without hitting the cube top.<br/></li><li><br/><strong>Material durability</strong>: Reinforced seams, sturdy mesh vents. Avoid thin fabric that tears.<br/></li><li><br/><strong>Connection options</strong>: If you want to link with tunnels or other cubes, check for connectors or zippers (like the Snarky Pets version).<br/></li><li><br/><strong>Fold-flat storage</strong>: If space is limited, look for cubes that collapse easily and can be moved under beds or closets.</li></ul>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_7jTBtL",
        "text_cE7LyU"
      ],
